timuli_ids": []}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "title": "", "id": 1, "type": "audio", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n2le03ob05re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n2le03ob05re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Stephen</span>: Hey, Amy! How are you doing? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: I'm fine! I'm studying for an exam about non-procedural languages and I'm worried about it! <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Stephen</span>: How come? They are very easy. I can help you study for that exam, Amy. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: Really? Thanks, Stephen. Well, what can you tell me about non-procedural languages? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Stephen</span>: First, a non-procedural language is what some programmers call Declarative Languages. They don't require to use traditional logic or steps to perform a task.  Second, non-procedural languages make people spend a little less time decoding and debugging programs.", "image": "enpe7n2le03ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "45000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: Nice, can you give me some examples of non-procedural languages? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Stephen</span>: Well, one of them is SQL. You can use this language for database management; most databases support SQL, therefore management and manipulation of data become reliable. Another example is PROLOG, which is a programming language for electronic devices. Next, we have HTML, which is another declarative language. People use it to create most web-pages; with HTML, you can work with different resources such as videos, images, texts, etc. Take into account that non-procedural languages focus more on the outcome rather than other things we usually take into consideration when using procedural languages.", "image": "enpe7n2le03ob05re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "102500", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: Wow! You know a lot about non-procedural languages. Let me see if I understood what non-procedural languages are. The idea of using non-procedural languages is to spend less time debugging and coding programs. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Stephen</span>: That's right! To conclude, a non-procedural language like WDSL describes the service language that interacts with catalogs and a language like XML develops modular vocabulary in an open format for data structures on the internet. These languages are very common, they indicate the computer what the user wants to obtain. It's very simple. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: Thanks, Stephen. You're a life saver.", "image": "enpe7n2le03ob05re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}]}}], "_data": []}], "id": 0}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Nonprocedural Languages"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear/use to talk about nonprocedural languages."}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand key information about the concepts, principles, and methodologies in simple spoken and written situations.  Talk about programming techniques, use cases, kinds, and sequences in simple spoken and written situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures.  Identifies general aspects related to Software Programming in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n2le03ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Subject and Object Pronouns Review"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\"> subject and object pronouns </span> to replace the noun in a sentence. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Subject pronouns </span>: We use subject pronouns to replace the subject of a sentence, this can be a person or thing. <br/><br/>  Example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\"> Carlos </span> knows a lot about nonprocedural languages, <span class=\"strong\"> he </span> is the best student of this class. </span><br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\"> Carlos </span> is the subject of the action and we can replace <span class=\"italic\"> Carlos</span>  with the <span class=\"strong\"> subject pronoun </span> <span class=\"italic\"> he</span>. <br/><br/>  <span class=\"strong\"> Object pronouns </span>:<br/> You use <span class=\"strong\"> object pronouns </span> instead of using nouns when the noun is the object of a sentence. <br/><br/>  Example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"> Peter learns about programming languages. Peter wants to know everything about <span class=\"strong\"> them </span>. </span><br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\"> Them</span>  replaces programming languages in the second sentence. <br/><br/>   Take a look at the following chart where your will see the <span class=\"strong\"> subject pronouns </span> and their <span class=\"strong\"> object pronoun </span>. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Subject pronouns</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Object pronouns</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Me\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Him\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Her\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Us\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Them\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Them\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "A non-procedural language is what some programmers call Declarative Languages. They don't require to use traditional logic or steps to perform a task."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Next, we have HTML, which is another declarative language. People use it to create most web-pages."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can you give me some examples of non-procedural languages? Well, one of them is SQL."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Connectors to Show Sequence"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\"> connectors </span> when you want to link two or more ideas."}, {"type": "text", "content": "We can use <span class=\"strong\"> connectors </span> to describe a <span class=\"strong\"> sequence </span> of ideas or actions. <br/> <br/>    Take a look at the following chart to see some of those <span class=\"strong\"> connectors </span>.<br/>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Type of Connector </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Example</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Ordinal numbers\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"First, second, third, etc.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sequence\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Then, next, after that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To conclude \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To sum up, finally, to conclude \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <br/>  <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">First</span>, we are going to talk about nonprocedural languages. <span class=\"strong\"> Then</span>, we need to see which language is the most common. <span class=\"strong\"> After that</span>, we are going to focus our attention on that language. <span class=\"strong\"> Finally</span>, we are going to use it. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "First, a non-procedural language is what some programmers call Declarative Languages."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Second, non-procedural languages make people spend a little less time decoding and debugging programs."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Next, we have HTML, which is another declarative language."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fine "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "admirable and excellent condition"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm fine! I'm studying for an exam about non-procedural languages and I'm worried about it!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n2le03ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "debug "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to clean bugs or small errors in programming"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Non-procedural languages make people spend a little less time decoding and debugging programs."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n2le03ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "reliable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "trustable performance"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Most databases support SQL, therefore management and manipulation of data become reliable."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n2le03ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "programming"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "language used for the creation, edition and development of programs"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Another example is PROLOG, which is a programming language for electronic devices."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n2le03ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "web-pages "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a document that  is part of the World Wide Web"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Next, we have HTML, which is another declarative language. People use it to create most web-pages."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n2le03ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about types of NPL and their use"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a short text describing each one. Don't forget to use the grammar studied"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss your work with your partners"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I can look for information about types of NPL and their use"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can write a short text describing each one using the grammar studied"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can discuss my work with my partners"}]}]}